Race Traits ~ Umbragen	CATEGORY:Internal	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=Umbragen Race Trait
Drow Heritage	KEY:Umbragen ~ Drow Heritage	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Umbragen Race Trait.Race Trait.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.48	DESC:Umbragen are drow and have all drow racial traits except as noted: darkvision 120 ft., immunity to sleep, +2 racial bonus on saves against enchantments, spell resistance 11 + class level, light blindness, and +2 on Listen, Search, and Spot (noticing secret doors within 5 feet).
Shadow Bond	KEY:Umbragen ~ Shadow Bond	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Umbragen Race Trait.Race Trait.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.48	DESC:+2 racial bonus on Hide and Move Silently checks (replaces the drow bonus on saves against spells and spell-like abilities).
Weapon Proficiency	KEY:Umbragen ~ Weapon Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Umbragen Race Trait.Race Trait.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.48	DESC:Proficient with longbow, shortbow, longsword, and rapier (replaces the drow weapon proficiencies).
Spell-Like Abilities	KEY:Umbragen ~ Spell-Like Abilities	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Umbragen Race Trait.Race Trait.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.48	DESC:1/day dancing lights, darkness, and faerie fire (caster level equals class level).
Light Blindness	KEY:Umbragen ~ Light Blindness	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Umbragen Race Trait.Race Trait.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.48	DESC:Abrupt exposure to bright light blinds for 1 round; afterward, dazzled while in bright light.

###Block: Insectare
Race Traits ~ Insectare	CATEGORY:Internal	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=Insectare Race Trait
Antenna Rake	KEY:Insectare ~ Antenna Rake	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Insectare Race Trait.Race Trait.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.52	DESC:Two antenna attacks per round, treated as off-hand weapons (1d4 slashing + 1/2 Strength bonus each), or one antenna as an attack action at the normal bonus.
Chitin Plates	KEY:Insectare ~ Chitin Plates	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Insectare Race Trait.Race Trait.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.52	DESC:+2 natural armor bonus.
Deceptive	KEY:Insectare ~ Deceptive	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Insectare Race Trait.Race Trait.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.52	DESC:+2 racial bonus on Bluff and Disguise checks.
Elven Blood	KEY:Insectare ~ Elven Blood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Insectare Race Trait.Race Trait.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.52	DESC:Counts as an elf for all race-related effects.

###Block: Shared race helpers
Racial Ability Bonus	KEY:DMC ~ Racial Ability Bonus	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Race Trait.SpecialQuality	MULT:YES	STACK:NO	CHOOSE:PCSTAT|ALL	BONUS:STAT|%LIST|2|TYPE=Racial	DESC:+2 racial bonus to a chosen ability score.	SOURCEPAGE:p.31

###Block: Saurian shifter traits (choose one; toggle the 'Saurian Shifting' temporary bonus to apply)
Saurian Shifting Tracker	CATEGORY:Internal	DEFINE:SaurianShifting|0	TEMPBONUS:PC|VAR|SaurianShifting|1	PRERACE:1,Saurian Shifter
Beasthide	KEY:Saurian Shifter Trait ~ Beasthide	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SaurianShifterTrait.Supernatural.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.48	PRERACE:1,Saurian Shifter	DESC:(Su) +2 Constitution and +2 natural armor bonus while shifting.	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|Saurian Shifting Tracker	BONUS:STAT|CON|2|PREVAREQ:SaurianShifting,1	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|2|TYPE=NaturalArmor.STACK|PREVAREQ:SaurianShifting,1
Broadwing	KEY:Saurian Shifter Trait ~ Broadwing	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SaurianShifterTrait.Supernatural.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.48	PRERACE:1,Saurian Shifter	DESC:(Su) +2 Dexterity while shifting; falls are treated as 40 feet shorter for damage.	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|Saurian Shifting Tracker	BONUS:STAT|DEX|2|PREVAREQ:SaurianShifting,1
Junglerunner	KEY:Saurian Shifter Trait ~ Junglerunner	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SaurianShifterTrait.Supernatural.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.48	PRERACE:1,Saurian Shifter	DESC:(Su) +2 Dexterity and +20 ft. base land speed while shifting.	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|Saurian Shifting Tracker	BONUS:STAT|DEX|2|PREVAREQ:SaurianShifting,1	BONUS:MOVEADD|TYPE.Walk|20|PREVAREQ:SaurianShifting,1
Longtooth	KEY:Saurian Shifter Trait ~ Longtooth	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SaurianShifterTrait.Supernatural.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.48	PRERACE:1,Saurian Shifter	DESC:(Su) +2 Strength while shifting and a bite attack dealing 1d6 (+1 per four character levels). One bite per round; usable as a secondary attack (-5) while wielding a weapon.	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|Saurian Shifting Tracker	BONUS:STAT|STR|2|PREVAREQ:SaurianShifting,1
Raptorleap	KEY:Saurian Shifter Trait ~ Raptorleap	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SaurianShifterTrait.Supernatural.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.48	PRERACE:1,Saurian Shifter	DESC:(Su) +2 Strength and +4 bonus on Jump checks while shifting; all Jump checks count as having a running start.	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|Saurian Shifting Tracker	BONUS:STAT|STR|2|PREVAREQ:SaurianShifting,1	BONUS:SKILL|Jump|4|PREVAREQ:SaurianShifting,1
Razorclaw	KEY:Saurian Shifter Trait ~ Razorclaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SaurianShifterTrait.Supernatural.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.48	PRERACE:1,Saurian Shifter	DESC:(Su) +2 Strength while shifting and two claws dealing 1d4 (+1 per four character levels) as primary natural weapons; one claw can be used as a light off-hand weapon (-2 on all attacks that round).	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|Saurian Shifting Tracker	BONUS:STAT|STR|2|PREVAREQ:SaurianShifting,1
Widetail	KEY:Saurian Shifter Trait ~ Widetail	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SaurianShifterTrait.Supernatural.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.48	PRERACE:1,Saurian Shifter	DESC:(Su) +2 Constitution while shifting and a tail slap dealing 1d6 bludgeoning (+1 per four character levels). One slap per round; usable as a secondary attack (-5) while wielding a weapon.	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|Saurian Shifting Tracker	BONUS:STAT|CON|2|PREVAREQ:SaurianShifting,1

###Block: Remade (output abilities)
Remade	KEY:Remade	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.67	DESC:Inherited template. Body reshaped in the punishment factories of New Crobuzon. Gains enhancements and an equal number of defects, chosen by the DM or rolled; apply them as separate 'Remade:' templates. No construct traits. Level adjustment: base creature +1.
Aquatic Prosthesis	KEY:Remade ~ Aquatic Prosthesis	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.68	DESC:Remade enhancement. +4 bonus on checks and saves against drowning or poison gas; +10 ft. swim speed (or a 10 ft. swim speed if none).
Armored Integument	KEY:Remade ~ Armored Integument	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.68	DESC:Remade enhancement. +1 natural armor.
Consummate Eyes	KEY:Remade ~ Consummate Eyes	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.68	DESC:Remade enhancement. +4 racial bonus on Search and Spot checks.
Metaclockwork	KEY:Remade ~ Metaclockwork	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.68	DESC:Remade enhancement. A metaclockwork device replicates three 0-level cleric or wizard spells (chosen by the DM), for a combined total of three uses per day.
Night Vision	KEY:Remade ~ Night Vision	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.68	DESC:Remade enhancement. +60 ft. darkvision (maximum 240 ft.).
Olfactory Enhancers	KEY:Remade ~ Olfactory Enhancers	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.68	DESC:Remade enhancement. Gains the scent special ability.
Spring-Loaded Jumper	KEY:Remade ~ Spring-Loaded Jumper	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.68	DESC:Remade enhancement. +4 bonus on Balance and Jump checks.
Supernumerary Arms	KEY:Remade ~ Supernumerary Arms	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.68	DESC:Remade enhancement. An awkward extra limb: +2 bonus on Climb checks and can hold an item under 5 pounds. Cannot wield weapons or provide extra magic item slots.
Supernumerary Legs	KEY:Remade ~ Supernumerary Legs	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.68	DESC:Remade enhancement. +5 ft. base speed and +4 bonus on checks to resist bull rush or trip.
Unnatural Weapon	KEY:Remade ~ Unnatural Weapon	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.68	DESC:Remade enhancement. A permanently attached weapon usable as a natural weapon. Damage by size: Diminutive 1, Tiny 1d2, Small 1d3, Medium 1d4, Large 1d6, Huge 1d8, Gargantuan 2d6, Colossal 3d6. PCGen entry assumes Medium (1d4).
Wakeful Engine	KEY:Remade ~ Wakeful Engine	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.68	DESC:Remade enhancement. Requires no rest to avoid fatigue or exhaustion (still needs rest to regain spells). Must also take the Boiler defect.
Boiler	KEY:Remade ~ Boiler	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.69	DESC:Remade defect. A steam boiler needing 2 gp of fuel per day. Out of fuel: immediately fatigued; each further day requires a Fortitude save (DC 14 + 1 per day) or become exhausted. Submersion extinguishes it. Adds 40 lb. of weight.
Clumsy	KEY:Remade ~ Clumsy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.69	DESC:Remade defect. -2 Dexterity.
Crippled Limb	KEY:Remade ~ Crippled Limb	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.69	DESC:Remade defect. One hand or arm is useless: cannot wield weapons with it, use two-handed weapons, or hold items.
Dulled Faculties (Listen)	KEY:Remade ~ Dulled Faculties (Listen)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.69	DESC:Remade defect. -4 penalty on Listen checks. (Choose two of the three Dulled Faculties templates.)
Dulled Faculties (Search)	KEY:Remade ~ Dulled Faculties (Search)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.69	DESC:Remade defect. -4 penalty on Search checks. (Choose two of the three Dulled Faculties templates.)
Dulled Faculties (Spot)	KEY:Remade ~ Dulled Faculties (Spot)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.69	DESC:Remade defect. -4 penalty on Spot checks. (Choose two of the three Dulled Faculties templates.)
Hideous Deformity	KEY:Remade ~ Hideous Deformity	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.69	DESC:Remade defect. -4 penalty on Diplomacy and Gather Information checks.
Malfunctioning Memories	KEY:Remade ~ Malfunctioning Memories	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.69	DESC:Remade defect. 25%% chance on each skill check to count only half your ranks (no effect on untrained checks).
Poor Healing	KEY:Remade ~ Poor Healing	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.69	DESC:Remade defect. Regains only one-quarter the normal hit points from natural healing (minimum 1 per day).
Slow	KEY:Remade ~ Slow	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.69	DESC:Remade defect. -10 ft. base speed.
Stiff Jointed	KEY:Remade ~ Stiff Jointed	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.69	DESC:Remade defect. -4 penalty on Balance, Jump, and Tumble checks.
Wheels	KEY:Remade ~ Wheels	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Remade.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.69	DESC:Remade defect. Needs a DC 14 Strength check to move through rough terrain; cannot charge or run on uneven ground; Strength checks to climb stairs (DC 15) or ladders (DC 20) per 10 feet; -4 on Swim and Ride checks.


###Block: Class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Master ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Master Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=ArmorProfLight|TYPE=ShieldProf|TYPE=WeaponProfSimple	SOURCEPAGE:p.346	DESC:Masters are proficient with all simple weapons. Masters are proficient with light armor and with shields (but not tower shields).
Primary Focus	KEY:Master ~ Primary Focus	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Master Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Master Primary Focus|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.346	DESC:At 1st level, masters choose which broad category of talents they are most proficient in, out of the four given below (craftsman, performer, professional, sage). This becomes their primary focus, and determines their class skills, and which focus group they may select their knacks from as they advance. In addition, masters add a +2 competence bonus to all skill checks made with their key skill (Craft, Perform, Profession, or Knowledge).
Knack	KEY:Master ~ Knack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Master Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Master Knack|floor((MasterLVL+2)/3)	SOURCEPAGE:p.347	DESC:Beginning at 1st level, masters acquire specific abilities as they advance, which belong to groups associated with the four master foci. These abilities are known as knacks. Some knacks have prerequisites, which must be met before they can be taken. Some knacks can be taken only once, while others may be taken multiple times, with cumulative effects. Masters may choose knacks only from a list associated with their primary or secondary focus. (Knacks at 1st, 4th, 7th, 10th, 13th, 16th and 19th level.)
Bonus Feat	KEY:Master ~ Bonus Feat	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Master Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:Pool_MasterFeat|0	BONUS:VAR|Pool_MasterFeat|floor((MasterLVL+1)/3)	SOURCEPAGE:p.347	DESC:At 2nd level and at every 3 levels thereafter (5th, 8th, 11th, 14th, 17th and 20th), the master gains a bonus feat, which must be selected from the following list: Acrobatic, Agile, Alertness, Animal Affinity, Athletic, Deceitful, Deft Hands, Diligent, Greater Improvise Weapon, Improvise Weapon, Investigator, Magical Aptitude, Negotiator, Nimble Fingers, Persuasive, Self-Sufficient, Skill Focus, Stealthy.
Secondary Focus	KEY:Master ~ Secondary Focus	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Master Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Master Secondary Focus|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.347	DESC:At 7th level masters may add a secondary focus from one of the other categories they have not yet selected as their primary focus, adding that category's class skills to their own class skill list and gaining a +2 competence bonus to the key skill of the new category. The competence bonus to the master's primary focus key skill increases to +4.
Skill Mastery	KEY:Master ~ Skill Mastery	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Master Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Skill Mastery|3+INT	SOURCEPAGE:p.347	DESC:At 10th level, masters select a number of skills from their class list equal to 3 + their Intelligence modifier. When making a skill check using one of these skills, masters may take 10 even if stress and distractions would normally prevent them from doing so.
Craftsman	KEY:Master Primary Focus ~ Craftsman	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterPrimaryFocus.SpecialQuality	CSKILL:Appraise|TYPE=Craft|Diplomacy|Disable Device|Forgery|Knowledge (Architecture and Engineering)|Knowledge (Local)|Listen|Open Lock|Search|Sense Motive|Spot|Use Rope	BONUS:SKILL|TYPE=Craft|min(4,2+2*floor(MasterLVL/7))|TYPE=Competence	SOURCEPAGE:p.346	DESC:Masters who choose the craftsman focus are dedicated to producing exceptional quality workmanship, from blacksmithing to bookbinding. Master craftsmen are skilled inventors and artisans. Craft is the master craftsman's key skill. Class skills: Appraise, Craft, Diplomacy, Disable Device, Forgery, Knowledge (Architecture and Engineering), Knowledge (Local), Listen, Open Lock, Search, Sense Motive, Spot, Use Rope. +2 competence bonus on Craft checks (+4 from 7th level).
Craftsman	KEY:Master Secondary Focus ~ Craftsman	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterSecondaryFocus.SpecialQuality	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Craftsman	CSKILL:Appraise|TYPE=Craft|Diplomacy|Disable Device|Forgery|Knowledge (Architecture and Engineering)|Knowledge (Local)|Listen|Open Lock|Search|Sense Motive|Spot|Use Rope	BONUS:SKILL|TYPE=Craft|2|TYPE=Competence	SOURCEPAGE:p.347	DESC:Masters who choose the craftsman focus are dedicated to producing exceptional quality workmanship, from blacksmithing to bookbinding. Master craftsmen are skilled inventors and artisans. Craft is the master craftsman's key skill. As a secondary focus: adds these class skills and a +2 competence bonus on Craft checks.
Performer	KEY:Master Primary Focus ~ Performer	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterPrimaryFocus.SpecialQuality	CSKILL:Balance|Bluff|Diplomacy|Intimidate|Knowledge (History)|Knowledge (Nobility and Royalty)|Listen|Move Silently|TYPE=Perform|Sleight of Hand|Speak Language|Spot|Tumble	BONUS:SKILL|TYPE=Perform|min(4,2+2*floor(MasterLVL/7))|TYPE=Competence	SOURCEPAGE:p.346	DESC:Masters who choose the performer focus are dedicated to creating exceptional performances, whether in art, music, or the stage. Master performers are talented actors and minstrels. Perform is the master performer's key skill. Class skills: Balance, Bluff, Diplomacy, Intimidate, Knowledge (History), Knowledge (Nobility and Royalty), Listen, Move Silently, Perform, Sleight of Hand, Speak Language, Spot, Tumble. +2 competence bonus on Perform checks (+4 from 7th level).
Performer	KEY:Master Secondary Focus ~ Performer	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterSecondaryFocus.SpecialQuality	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Performer	CSKILL:Balance|Bluff|Diplomacy|Intimidate|Knowledge (History)|Knowledge (Nobility and Royalty)|Listen|Move Silently|TYPE=Perform|Sleight of Hand|Speak Language|Spot|Tumble	BONUS:SKILL|TYPE=Perform|2|TYPE=Competence	SOURCEPAGE:p.347	DESC:Masters who choose the performer focus are dedicated to creating exceptional performances, whether in art, music, or the stage. Master performers are talented actors and minstrels. Perform is the master performer's key skill. As a secondary focus: adds these class skills and a +2 competence bonus on Perform checks.
Professional	KEY:Master Primary Focus ~ Professional	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterPrimaryFocus.SpecialQuality	CSKILL:Appraise|Bluff|Diplomacy|Gather Information|Handle Animal|Heal|Knowledge (Local)|Knowledge (Nature)|Listen|TYPE=Profession|Ride|Sense Motive|Survival	BONUS:SKILL|TYPE=Profession|min(4,2+2*floor(MasterLVL/7))|TYPE=Competence	SOURCEPAGE:p.346	DESC:Masters who choose the professional focus are dedicated to providing exceptional service, from money lending to bartending. Master professionals are savvy merchants and guides. Profession is the master professional's key skill. Class skills: Appraise, Bluff, Diplomacy, Gather Information, Handle Animal, Heal, Knowledge (Local), Knowledge (Nature), Listen, Profession, Ride, Sense Motive, Survival. +2 competence bonus on Profession checks (+4 from 7th level).
Professional	KEY:Master Secondary Focus ~ Professional	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterSecondaryFocus.SpecialQuality	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Professional	CSKILL:Appraise|Bluff|Diplomacy|Gather Information|Handle Animal|Heal|Knowledge (Local)|Knowledge (Nature)|Listen|TYPE=Profession|Ride|Sense Motive|Survival	BONUS:SKILL|TYPE=Profession|2|TYPE=Competence	SOURCEPAGE:p.347	DESC:Masters who choose the professional focus are dedicated to providing exceptional service, from money lending to bartending. Master professionals are savvy merchants and guides. Profession is the master professional's key skill. As a secondary focus: adds these class skills and a +2 competence bonus on Profession checks.
Sage	KEY:Master Primary Focus ~ Sage	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterPrimaryFocus.SpecialQuality	CSKILL:Concentration|Decipher Script|Diplomacy|Forgery|Gather Information|Heal|TYPE=Knowledge|Ride|Search|Speak Language|Spellcraft|Use Magic Device	BONUS:SKILL|TYPE=Knowledge|min(4,2+2*floor(MasterLVL/7))|TYPE=Competence	SOURCEPAGE:p.346	DESC:Masters who choose the sage focus are dedicated to uncovering exceptional knowledge, from politics and history to engineering and the natural world. Master sages are learned scholars and counselors. Knowledge is the master sage's key skill. Class skills: Concentration, Decipher Script, Diplomacy, Forgery, Gather Information, Heal, Knowledge, Ride, Search, Speak Language, Spellcraft, Use Magic Device. +2 competence bonus on Knowledge checks (+4 from 7th level).
Sage	KEY:Master Secondary Focus ~ Sage	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterSecondaryFocus.SpecialQuality	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Sage	CSKILL:Concentration|Decipher Script|Diplomacy|Forgery|Gather Information|Heal|TYPE=Knowledge|Ride|Search|Speak Language|Spellcraft|Use Magic Device	BONUS:SKILL|TYPE=Knowledge|2|TYPE=Competence	SOURCEPAGE:p.347	DESC:Masters who choose the sage focus are dedicated to uncovering exceptional knowledge, from politics and history to engineering and the natural world. Master sages are learned scholars and counselors. Knowledge is the master sage's key skill. As a secondary focus: adds these class skills and a +2 competence bonus on Knowledge checks.
Applied Craftsmanship	KEY:Master Knack ~ Applied Craftsmanship	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.CraftsmanKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Craftsman],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Craftsman]	SOURCEPAGE:p.347	DESC:Master craftsmen have learned to apply their understanding of their craft to other crafts. With this knack, they may substitute ranks in a Craft skill for ranks in another Craft in which they have no ranks, on a two for one basis for the purposes of making Craft checks. For example, master craftsmen with 10 ranks in Craft (blacksmith) may attempt a Craft (leatherworking) check as if they had 5 ranks in that skill. Ability bonuses and other modifiers are applied as usual.
Word of Mouth	KEY:Master Knack ~ Word of Mouth	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.CraftsmanKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Craftsman],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Craftsman]	MULT:YES	STACK:NO	CHOOSE:SKILL|TYPE=Craft	SOURCEPAGE:p.347	DESC:The master craftsman's skill at his craft becomes widely known. Select a Craft skill. With this knack, a week's worth of dedicated work earns the master craftsman a number of steel pieces equal to his Craft check, rather than half his Craft check. This knack may be taken more than once. Each time, it applies to a different Craft skill.
Item of Distinction	KEY:Master Knack ~ Item of Distinction	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.CraftsmanKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Craftsman],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Craftsman]	PRESKILL:1,TYPE.Craft=3	MULT:YES	STACK:NO	CHOOSE:SKILL|TYPE=Craft	SOURCEPAGE:p.347	DESC:With this knack, the master craftsman learns how to more efficiently create masterwork items. Select a Craft skill. Masterwork items created with this Craft skill are known as items of distinction. Items of distinction function like other masterwork items, but the additional cost to create them is halved. An item of distinction can be recognized as such with a successful DC 15 Appraise check. This knack can be taken more than once. Each time, it applies to a different Craft skill. Prerequisite: Craft (specific skill) 3 ranks.
Item of Renown	KEY:Master Knack ~ Item of Renown	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.CraftsmanKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Craftsman],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Craftsman]	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Knack ~ Item of Distinction	PRESKILL:1,TYPE.Craft=6	SOURCEPAGE:p.347	DESC:With this knack, the master craftsman improves upon his existing talent at creating superior masterwork items. The master craftsman can create masterwork items that are twice as effective as standard masterwork items - weapons confer a +2 bonus to attack rolls, armor check penalty is lessened by 2, and skill bonus items confer a +4 bonus. These items must be created with the Craft skill specified by the master's item of distinction knack, take twice as long to create, and cost the same amount as standard masterwork items. Prerequisites: Item of Distinction, Craft (specific skill) 6 ranks.
Item of Fame	KEY:Master Knack ~ Item of Fame	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.CraftsmanKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Craftsman],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Craftsman]	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Knack ~ Item of Renown	PRESKILL:1,TYPE.Craft=9	SOURCEPAGE:p.347	DESC:With this knack, the master craftsman improves upon his existing talent at creating superior masterwork items. The master craftsman can create masterwork items that are three times as effective as standard masterwork items - weapons confer a +3 bonus to attack rolls, armor check penalty is lessened by 3, and skill bonus items confer a +6 bonus. These items must be created with the Craft skill specified by the master's item of distinction knack, take three times as long to create, and the additional cost to create them is tripled (+900 steel for weapons of fame, +450 steel for armor of fame, etc). Prerequisites: Item of Renown, Craft (specific skill) 9 ranks.
Item of Glory	KEY:Master Knack ~ Item of Glory	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.CraftsmanKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Craftsman],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Craftsman]	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Knack ~ Item of Fame	PRESKILL:1,TYPE.Craft=12	SOURCEPAGE:p.347	DESC:With this knack, the master craftsman improves upon his existing talent at creating superior masterwork items. The master craftsman can create masterwork items that are four times as effective as standard masterwork items - weapons confer a +4 bonus to attack rolls, armor check penalty is lessened by 4, and skill bonus items confer a +8 bonus. These items must be created with the Craft skill specified by the master's item of distinction knack, take four times as long to create, and the additional cost to create them is quadrupled (+1200 steel for weapons of glory, +600 steel for armor of glory, etc). Prerequisites: Item of Fame, Craft (specific skill) 12 ranks.
Item of Legend	KEY:Master Knack ~ Item of Legend	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.CraftsmanKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Craftsman],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Craftsman]	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Knack ~ Item of Glory	PRESKILL:1,TYPE.Craft=15	SOURCEPAGE:p.348	DESC:With this knack, the master craftsman improves upon his existing talent at creating superior masterwork items. The master craftsman can create masterwork items that are five times as effective as standard masterwork items - weapons confer a +5 bonus to attack rolls, armor check penalty is lessened by 5, and skill bonus items confer a +10 bonus. These items must be created with the Craft skill specified by the master's item of distinction knack, take five times as long to create, and the additional cost to create them is quintupled (+1500 steel for weapons of legend, +750 steel for armor of legend, etc). Prerequisites: Item of Glory, Craft (specific skill) 15 ranks.
Celebrity	KEY:Master Knack ~ Celebrity	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.PerformerKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Performer],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Performer]	MULT:YES	STACK:NO	CHOOSE:SKILL|TYPE=Perform	SOURCEPAGE:p.348	DESC:The master performer has achieved a certain level of widespread fame. Select a Perform skill. With this knack, the master performer's talents are able to command a higher price for performances with that skill. The master performer can earn twice the amount listed for an evening's work based on her Perform check result. This knack may be taken more than once. Each time, it applies to a different Perform skill.
Coordinate	KEY:Master Knack ~ Coordinate	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.PerformerKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Performer],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Performer]	PRESKILL:1,Diplomacy=3	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	TEMPBONUS:ANYPC|COMBAT|TOHIT|1|TYPE=Circumstance	TEMPBONUS:ANYPC|SKILL|ALL|1|TYPE=Circumstance	TEMPDESC:Allies coordinated by the master performer (+1 per selection of this knack)	SOURCEPAGE:p.348	DESC:The master performer has a knack for getting people to work together. When the master performer can spend a full round directing his allies and makes a DC 10 Diplomacy check, the performer provides any of his allies within 30 feet a +1 bonus on their attack rolls and skill checks. The bonus lasts for a number of rounds equal to the master performer's Charisma modifier. The master performer can coordinate a number of allies equal to one-half his master level, rounded down (to a minimum of one ally). This knack can be taken more than once. The bonuses on attack rolls and skill checks stack, and the number of rounds the bonuses last increases by +1 for each additional selection. Prerequisite: Diplomacy 3 ranks.
Inspiration	KEY:Master Knack ~ Inspiration	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.PerformerKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Performer],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Performer]	PRESKILL:1,TYPE.Perform=3	TEMPBONUS:ANYPC|SAVE|ALL|2|TYPE=Morale	TEMPBONUS:ANYPC|COMBAT|TOHIT|2|TYPE=Morale	TEMPBONUS:ANYPC|COMBAT|DAMAGE|2|TYPE=Morale	TEMPDESC:Allies inspired by the master performer (not the master himself)	SOURCEPAGE:p.348	DESC:The master performer can inspire allies with performances, bolstering them and improving their chances of success. An ally must listen to and observe the master performer for a full round for the inspiration to take hold, and the character must make a DC 15 Perform check. The effect lasts for a number of rounds equal to the character's Charisma modifier. An inspired ally gains a +2 morale bonus on saving throws, attack rolls, and damage rolls. A master performer cannot inspire himself. The character can inspire a number of allies equal to one-half of his master performer level, rounded down (to a minimum of one ally). Prerequisite: Perform 3 ranks.
Greater Inspiration	KEY:Master Knack ~ Greater Inspiration	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.PerformerKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Performer],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Performer]	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Knack ~ Inspiration	PRESKILL:1,TYPE.Perform=6	TEMPBONUS:ANYPC|SAVE|ALL|3|TYPE=Morale	TEMPBONUS:ANYPC|COMBAT|TOHIT|3|TYPE=Morale	TEMPBONUS:ANYPC|COMBAT|DAMAGE|3|TYPE=Morale	TEMPDESC:Allies under greater inspiration (total +3 morale; use instead of Inspiration)	SOURCEPAGE:p.348	DESC:The master performer can inspire allies to even greater heights with performances, bolstering them and improving their chances of success. An ally must listen to and observe the master performer for a full round for the greater inspiration to take hold, and the hero must make a DC 15 Perform check. The effect lasts for a number of rounds equal to the character's Charisma modifier. An inspired ally gains an additional +1 morale bonus on saving throws, attack rolls, and damage rolls, which stacks with the bonus from inspiration for a total of a +3 morale bonus. A master performer cannot inspire himself. The character can inspire a number of allies equal to one-half his master performer level, rounded down (to a minimum of one ally). Prerequisites: Inspiration, Perform 6 ranks.
Compelling Performance	KEY:Master Knack ~ Compelling Performance	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.PerformerKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Performer],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Performer]	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Knack ~ Greater Inspiration	PRESKILL:1,TYPE.Perform=12	SOURCEPAGE:p.348	DESC:With this knack, the master performer's skill has increased to the point that he can arouse a single emotion of his choice - despair, hope, or rage - in a target. The master performer can use this ability a number of times per day equal to his Charisma bonus (if any). The emotion the master performer arouses affects one target within 15 feet. The performance requires a full-round action and a Perform skill check, and its effects on the target last for 1d4+1 rounds. The target makes a Will saving throw. The DC is equal to the master performer's Perform skill check. An unfriendly target gains a +5 bonus to his Will saving throw, while a hostile target gains a +10 bonus. If the target succeeds at the saving throw, the master performer is immune to the compulsion of this performance. If the target fails, the master performer reacts to the emotion as described below. Despair: The target takes a -2 morale penalty on saving throws, attack rolls, ability checks, skill checks, and weapon damage rolls. Hope: The target gains a +2 morale bonus on saving throws, attack rolls, ability checks, skill checks, and weapon damage rolls. Rage: The target gains a +2 morale bonus to Strength and Constitution, a +1 morale bonus on Will saves, and a -2 penalty to Armor Class. In a dramatic situation, the target is compelled to fight, regardless of the danger. Prerequisites: Greater Inspiration, Perform 12 ranks.
Virtuoso	KEY:Master Knack ~ Virtuoso	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.PerformerKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Performer],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Performer]	SOURCEPAGE:p.348	DESC:The master performer has learned how to apply talents in one technique to another. With this knack, the master performer may substitute ranks in a Perform skill for ranks in another Perform skill in which the master performer has no ranks on a two for one basis for the purposes of making Perform checks. For example, a master performer with 10 ranks in Perform (wind instruments) may attempt a Perform (comedy) check as if he had 5 ranks in that skill. Ability bonuses and other modifiers are applied as usual. Skills such as Sleight-of-Hand and Tumble may not be mimicked with this knack.
Fast-Talk	KEY:Master Knack ~ Fast-Talk	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.ProfessionalKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Professional],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Professional]	TEMPBONUS:PC|SKILL|Bluff,Diplomacy,Disguise|floor(MasterLVL/2)|TYPE=Competence	TEMPDESC:Bluff, Diplomacy or Disguise checks to lie, cheat or otherwise bend the truth	SOURCEPAGE:p.349	DESC:The master professional has a way with words when attempting to con and deceive. With this knack, he applies half his master level (round down) as a competence bonus on any Bluff, Diplomacy, or Disguise checks he makes while attempting to lie, cheat, or otherwise bend the truth.
Bluster	KEY:Master Knack ~ Bluster	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.ProfessionalKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Professional],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Professional]	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Knack ~ Fast-Talk	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	SOURCEPAGE:p.349	DESC:The master professional has the ability to bluster a target through sheer force of personality, a winning smile, and fast-talking. The target must have an Intelligence score of 3 or higher to be susceptible to a bluster attempt, must be within 30 feet of the master professional, and must be able to see, hear, and understand him. To bluster a target, the master professional uses a standard action and makes a Bluff check opposed by the target's Sense Motive check. If the Bluff check succeeds, the target receives a -1 penalty on attack rolls, ability checks, skill checks, and saving throws for a number of rounds equal to the character's Charisma bonus (if positive). This knack can be selected multiple times, each time worsening the penalty by -1. This is a mind-affecting ability. Prerequisite: Fast-Talk.
Faithful Aide	KEY:Master Knack ~ Faithful Aide	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.ProfessionalKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Professional],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Professional]	PRESKILL:1,TYPE.Profession=7	SOURCEPAGE:p.349	DESC:The master professional has acquired a talented apprentice, student, bodyguard, or servant. This knack functions like the Leadership feat, but it applies only to a cohort, and the master professional's Leadership score is equal to his ranks in a chosen Profession skill plus his Charisma bonus. The aide can be a character of any class, although usually another master, and is treated exactly as any other cohort. Prerequisite: Profession 7 ranks.
Jack of All Trades	KEY:Master Knack ~ Jack of All Trades	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.ProfessionalKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Professional],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Professional]	SOURCEPAGE:p.349	DESC:The master professional has learned how to apply his experience and savvy with one area of professional expertise in order to succeed in others. With this knack, he may substitute ranks in a Profession skill for ranks in another Profession skill in which he has no ranks. These may be substituted on a two for one basis for the purposes of making Profession checks. For example, a master professional with 10 ranks in Profession (merchant) may attempt a Profession (innkeeper) check as if he had 5 ranks in that skill. Ability bonuses and other modifiers are applied as usual. Use of this knack does not confer synergy bonuses to other skills.
Loyal Clientele	KEY:Master Knack ~ Loyal Clientele	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.ProfessionalKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Professional],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Professional]	MULT:YES	STACK:NO	CHOOSE:SKILL|TYPE=Profession	SOURCEPAGE:p.349	DESC:The master professional's skill at his trade becomes widely known. Select a Profession skill. With this knack, the master professional is able to command a higher price for his services with that skill. For a week's worth of dedicated work the master professional can earn a number of steel pieces equal to his Profession check, rather than half his Profession check. This knack may be taken more than once. Each time, it applies to a different Profession skill.
Skilled Team	KEY:Master Knack ~ Skilled Team	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.ProfessionalKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Professional],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Professional]	PRESKILL:1,TYPE.Profession=10	SOURCEPAGE:p.349	DESC:The master professional has gathered a small group of apprentices and helpers who assist him in his work. This knack functions like the Leadership feat, but it applies only to followers and the master professional's Leadership score is equal to his ranks in a chosen Profession skill plus his Charisma bonus. These assistants are all NPC experts, and are otherwise treated exactly like followers. Prerequisite: Profession 10 ranks.
Academic Reputation	KEY:Master Knack ~ Academic Reputation	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.SageKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Sage],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Sage]	SOURCEPAGE:p.349	DESC:The master sage's knowledge and learning can guarantee a substantial amount of fame and income. With this knack, the master sage may add his Intelligence bonus to any Bluff, Diplomacy, or Intimidate checks relating to a Knowledge skill in which the master sage has at least 4 ranks, instead of his Charisma bonus. In addition, the master sage may earn a number of steel pieces equal to his Knowledge skill check for each week of dedicated work as a consultant, scholar, and sage, much as a character with Perform, Craft or Profession earns money with his skill.
Complementary Scholarship	KEY:Master Knack ~ Complementary Scholarship	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.SageKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Sage],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Sage]	SOURCEPAGE:p.349	DESC:The master sage has learned how to apply his understanding of his existing fields of knowledge to other fields. With this knack, the master sage may substitute ranks in a Knowledge skill for ranks in another Knowledge skill in which he has no ranks on a two for one basis for the purposes of making Knowledge checks. For example, a master sage with 10 ranks in Knowledge (nobility) may attempt a Knowledge (history) check as if he had 5 ranks in that skill. Ability bonuses and other modifiers are applied as usual. Use of this knack does not confer synergy bonuses to other skills.
Exploit Weakness	KEY:Master Knack ~ Exploit Weakness	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.SageKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Sage],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Sage]	SOURCEPAGE:p.349	DESC:After 1 round of combat, the master sage can designate one opponent and try to find ways to gain an advantage by using brains over brawn. The master sage uses a move action and makes a DC 15 Intelligence check with a bonus equal to half his class level. If the check succeeds, for the rest of the combat the master sage uses his Intelligence bonus instead of either Strength or Dexterity bonus on attack rolls as he finds ways to outthink his opponent and notices weaknesses in his opponent's fighting style.
Linguist	KEY:Master Knack ~ Linguist	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.SageKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Sage],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Sage]	PRELANG:4,ANY	SOURCEPAGE:p.349	DESC:With this knack, the master sage becomes an exceptional linguist. Whenever the character encounters a new language that he does not know, the master sage can make an Intelligence check to determine if he can understand it. The check is made with a bonus equal to half the character's master level (rounded up). For a written language, the bonus applies to a Decipher Script check instead. The DC for the check depends on the situation: DC 15 if the language is related to a language the sage already knows; DC 20 if the language is unrelated to any other languages the sage knows; and DC 25 if the language is ancient or unique. The master sage can glean enough meaning from a conversation or document to ascertain the basic message, but this ability in no way is equivalent to actually being able to converse or fluently read and write in a given language. A single check covers roughly one minute of a spoken language or one page of a written language. Prerequisite: Knowledge of at least 3 different languages apart from the master sage's native language.
Lore	KEY:Master Knack ~ Lore	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.SageKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Sage],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Sage]	DEFINE:BardicKnowledgeLVL|0	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Bardic Knowledge	BONUS:VAR|BardicKnowledgeLVL|MasterLVL	SOURCEPAGE:p.350	DESC:With this knack, the master sage has acquired a talent for picking up assorted facts, historical trivia, and random legends, just as a bard does with bardic knowledge. The master sage adds his class level and his Intelligence modifier to the lore check, which otherwise functions exactly like a bardic knowledge check. The master sage's levels stack with other classes which have bardic knowledge checks, such as the bard or loremaster, but not the mariner (whose sailor lore works differently).
Tactical Advantage	KEY:Master Knack ~ Tactical Advantage	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MasterKnack.SageKnack.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Primary Focus ~ Sage],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Secondary Focus ~ Sage]	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Master Knack ~ Exploit Weakness	MULT:YES	STACK:NO	CHOOSE:SKILL|TYPE=Knowledge	TEMPBONUS:PC|COMBAT|TOHIT|2|TYPE=Circumstance	TEMPDESC:Attacks against a creature covered by the chosen Knowledge skill, after a successful check (rest of the encounter)	SOURCEPAGE:p.350	DESC:By using his understanding of a creature's recorded weaknesses, the master sage can gain an advantage in combat. Choose a Knowledge skill to which this knack applies. Once per encounter, a master sage may make a Knowledge check (DC 10 + creature's HD) to gain a +2 bonus to attack rolls against a creature covered by the selected Knowledge skill for the remainder of the encounter. The specific Knowledge skill required depends on the creature type: Knowledge (arcana) for dragons, constructs, and magical beasts; Knowledge (dungeoneering) for aberrations and oozes; Knowledge (the planes) for elementals and outsiders; Knowledge (nature) for animals, fey, giants, monstrous humanoids, plants, and vermin; Knowledge (religion) for undead; Knowledge (local) for humanoids and regional cultures. This knack may be taken more than once. Each time it applies to a different Knowledge skill. Prerequisite: Exploit Weakness.


###Block: Domain granted powers and domain spell lists
Army	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain	SOURCEPAGE:p.1355	DESC:You have the spell-like ability to inspire allies within 30 feet, giving them a +2 morale bonus on saving throws, attack rolls, ability checks, skill checks, and weapon damage rolls. Allies must be able to hear you speak for 1 round. Using this ability is a full-round action. It lasts a number of rounds equal to your Charisma bonus and can be used once per day.|!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Internal,Remove Domain Power (Army)	ABILITY:Domain|AUTOMATIC|Domain Power ~ Army|!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Internal,Remove Domain Power (Army)	ABILITY:Domain|AUTOMATIC|Domain Spells ~ Army
Army	KEY:Domain Power ~ Army	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain Power	SOURCEPAGE:p.1355	DESC:You have the spell-like ability to inspire allies within 30 feet, giving them a +2 morale bonus on saving throws, attack rolls, ability checks, skill checks, and weapon damage rolls. Allies must be able to hear you speak for 1 round. Using this ability is a full-round action. It lasts a number of rounds equal to your Charisma bonus and can be used once per day.
Army	KEY:Domain Spells ~ Army	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain Spells	SPELLLEVEL:DOMAIN|Army=1|Bless|Army=2|Lighten Load|Army=3|Prayer|Army=4|Divination|Army=5|Easy March|Army=6|Heroes' Feast|Army=7|Scrying (Greater)|Army=8|Heal (Mass)|Army=9|Teleportation Circle	DESC:Domain spells: 1 Bless; 2 Lighten Load; 3 Prayer; 4 Divination; 5 Easy march; 6 Heroes' feast; 7 Scrying, Greater; 8 Heal, Mass; 9 Teleportation Circle &nl;Note: the compendium prints the Army and Avarice spell lists under each other's heading; they are swapped back here
Avarice	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain	SOURCEPAGE:p.1355	DESC:Once per day, as a standard action, you may determine the most valuable item within 30 feet. An item's value is determined by its listed gold-piece value. If you cannot see the most valuable item within range, you become aware of its general location (within 5 feet), but you gain no insight into what the item is. This ability does not tell you the gold piece value of an item.|!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Internal,Remove Domain Power (Avarice)	ABILITY:Domain|AUTOMATIC|Domain Power ~ Avarice|!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Internal,Remove Domain Power (Avarice)	ABILITY:Domain|AUTOMATIC|Domain Spells ~ Avarice
Avarice	KEY:Domain Power ~ Avarice	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain Power	SOURCEPAGE:p.1355	DESC:Once per day, as a standard action, you may determine the most valuable item within 30 feet. An item's value is determined by its listed gold-piece value. If you cannot see the most valuable item within range, you become aware of its general location (within 5 feet), but you gain no insight into what the item is. This ability does not tell you the gold piece value of an item.
Avarice	KEY:Domain Spells ~ Avarice	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain Spells	SPELLLEVEL:DOMAIN|Avarice=3|Locate Object|Avarice=4|Shrink Item|Avarice=5|Telekinesis|Avarice=6|Secret Chest|Avarice=7|Sequester|Avarice=8|Discern Location|Avarice=9|Antipathy	DESC:Domain spells: 1 Sticky Fingers; 2 Treasure Scent; 3 Locate Object; 4 Shrink Item; 5 Telekinesis; 6 Leomund's Secret Chest; 7 Sequester; 8 Discern Location; 9 Antipathy &nl;Note: the compendium prints the Army and Avarice spell lists under each other's heading; they are swapped back here
Beguilement	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain	SOURCEPAGE:p.1355	DESC:You cast compulsion spells at +1 caster level.|!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Internal,Remove Domain Power (Beguilement)	ABILITY:Domain|AUTOMATIC|Domain Power ~ Beguilement|!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Internal,Remove Domain Power (Beguilement)	ABILITY:Domain|AUTOMATIC|Domain Spells ~ Beguilement
Beguilement	KEY:Domain Power ~ Beguilement	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain Power	SOURCEPAGE:p.1355	DESC:You cast compulsion spells at +1 caster level.	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SUBSCHOOL.Compulsion|1|PRERULE:1,SYS_DOMAIN
Beguilement	KEY:Domain Spells ~ Beguilement	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain Spells	SPELLLEVEL:DOMAIN|Beguilement=1|Hypnotism|Beguilement=2|Enthrall|Beguilement=3|Hypnotic Pattern|Beguilement=4|Deep Slumber|Beguilement=5|Confusion|Beguilement=6|Modify Memory|Beguilement=7|Suggestion (Mass)|Beguilement=8|Hold Person (Mass)|Beguilement=9|Irresistible Dance	DESC:Domain spells: 1 Hypnotism; 2 Enthrall; 3 Hypnotic Pattern; 4 Deep Slumber; 5 Confusion; 6 Modify Memory; 7 Suggestion, Mass; 8 Hold Person, Mass; 9 Otto's Irresistible Dance
Charity	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain	SOURCEPAGE:p.1355	DESC:Once per day, as a full-round action, you may reduce your hit points by up two times your class level and touch an ally to give him temporary hit points equal to that amount. For instance, a 5th-level cleric can give up to 10 hit points to an ally. Your ally retains these temporary hit points for 1 minute per your class level and you cannot reclaim them or use healing magic to regain them prematurely, even to save your own life. At the end of the effect you regain all the hit points you donated, even if your ally suffered injuries during this time.|!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Internal,Remove Domain Power (Charity)	ABILITY:Domain|AUTOMATIC|Domain Power ~ Charity|!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Internal,Remove Domain Power (Charity)	ABILITY:Domain|AUTOMATIC|Domain Spells ~ Charity
Charity	KEY:Domain Power ~ Charity	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain Power	SOURCEPAGE:p.1355	DESC:Once per day, as a full-round action, you may reduce your hit points by up two times your class level and touch an ally to give him temporary hit points equal to that amount. For instance, a 5th-level cleric can give up to 10 hit points to an ally. Your ally retains these temporary hit points for 1 minute per your class level and you cannot reclaim them or use healing magic to regain them prematurely, even to save your own life. At the end of the effect you regain all the hit points you donated, even if your ally suffered injuries during this time.
Charity	KEY:Domain Spells ~ Charity	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain Spells	SPELLLEVEL:DOMAIN|Charity=1|Goodberry|Charity=2|Aid|Charity=3|Create Food and Water|Charity=4|Imbue with Spell Ability|Charity=5|Cure Light Wounds (Mass)|Charity=6|Heroes' Feast|Charity=7|Refuge|Charity=8|Mage's Magnificent Mansion|Charity=9|Heal (Mass)	DESC:Domain spells: 1 Goodberry; 2 Aid; 3 Create Food and Water; 4 Imbue with Spell Ability; 5 Cure Light Wounds, Mass; 6 Heroes' Feast; 7 Refuge; 8 Mordenkainen's Magnificent Mansion; 9 Heal, Mass
Chastity	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain	SOURCEPAGE:p.1356	DESC:Once per day, you may dispel a single spell effect targeting you as a targeted dispel magic spell. Caster level equals your character level.|!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Internal,Remove Domain Power (Chastity)	ABILITY:Domain|AUTOMATIC|Domain Power ~ Chastity|!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Internal,Remove Domain Power (Chastity)	ABILITY:Domain|AUTOMATIC|Domain Spells ~ Chastity
Chastity	KEY:Domain Power ~ Chastity	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain Power	SOURCEPAGE:p.1356	DESC:Once per day, you may dispel a single spell effect targeting you as a targeted dispel magic spell. Caster level equals your character level.
Chastity	KEY:Domain Spells ~ Chastity	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain Spells	SPELLLEVEL:DOMAIN|Chastity=1|Shield of Faith|Chastity=2|Restoration (Lesser)|Chastity=3|Magic Vestment|Chastity=4|Spell Immunity|Chastity=5|Break Enchantment|Chastity=6|Interposing Hand|Chastity=7|Repulsion|Chastity=8|Antimagic Field|Chastity=9|Mind Blank	DESC:Domain spells: 1 Shield of Faith; 2 Restoration, Lesser; 3 Magic Vestment; 4 Spell Immunity; 5 Break Enchantment; 6 Bigby's Interposing Hand; 7 Repulsion; 8 Antimagic Field; 9 Mind Blank
Chromatic Dragon	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain	SOURCEPAGE:p.1356	DESC:Choose a chromatic dragon color. You cannot later change the kind of dragon. Once per day, you may use a breath weapon similar to the chosen dragon's. This breath weapon deals 1d6 points of damage per five cleric levels you possess. A successful Reflex save (DC 10 + 1/2 your cleric level + your Charisma modifier) halves the damage. A black breathes a 60-foot line of acid, a blue breathes a 60-foot line of electricity, a green breathes a 30-foot cone of acid, a red breathes a 30-foot cone of fire, and a white breathes 30-foot cone of cold.|!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Internal,Remove Domain Power (Chromatic Dragon)	ABILITY:Domain|AUTOMATIC|Domain Power ~ Chromatic Dragon|!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Internal,Remove Domain Power (Chromatic Dragon)	ABILITY:Domain|AUTOMATIC|Domain Spells ~ Chromatic Dragon
